   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduce gender inequalities in Cuba through the implementation of a comprehensive care system with a gender-intersectional and gender-rights approach.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women are at the core of care works (unpaid) in the country, representing a significant domestic overload for them. This proposal ai ms to contribute to the design and implementation of a Comprehensive Care System from the gender-intersectional and gender-rights approach, as part of public protection and social security policies. This is presented as a necessity and one of the main challenges for Cuba in the current period. The project will foster the participation of caregivers in the generation of these policies, to ensure its direct impact on the well-being of women. The proposal also aims to promote a sociocultural environment that favours the positioning of the political and economic dimension of daily life, as well as the transformation of the ethical, social, economic and cultural challenges linked to care. Activities will be carried out by the representation of the United Nations Population Fund in Cuba and will take 3 years of implementation with a nation-wide impact.</narrative>
  </description>
